        "On a fresh SQLite database, the migration set auto-applies at boot — system/auth tables exist after startup",
        "On SQLite, a dynamic table declared in the schema is created and accepts a record-create request (201)",
        "On SQLite, a record round-trips: create → read → update → delete all succeed with the expected status codes",
        "On SQLite, Better Auth email/password sign-up succeeds and the new user is persisted",
        "On SQLite, sign-in with the signed-up credentials returns 200 with a session cookie",
        "On SQLite, a form submission persists a record that is subsequently readable via the records API",
        "On SQLite, `GET /api/admin/config/version` reports `runtime: \"sqlite-aio\"`",
        "On PostgreSQL, `GET /api/admin/config/version` reports `runtime: \"postgres\"`",
        "On SQLite, records created before a server restart against the same SQLite database file survive the restart and remain readable",
        "`DATABASE_URL=file:<path>` boots SQLite and creates the database file at the configured path; `/api/health` returns 200",
        "`DATABASE_URL=sqlite:<path>` (alias) boots SQLite identically — the file is created at the configured path",
        "An unknown `DATABASE_URL` scheme (e.g. `mysql://`) fails the server boot with `Unsupported DATABASE_URL scheme`",
        "A bare-path `DATABASE_URL` (no scheme, e.g. `./database.db`) fails the server boot — the operator must prefix it with `file:`",
        "A `postgresql://` `DATABASE_URL` still selects PostgreSQL after scheme discrimination (`runtime: \"postgres\"`) — the pg branch is unbroken",
        "On SQLite with `auth` configured AND a `created-by` field, the server boots and `/api/health` returns 200 — `ensureBetterAuthUsersTable` is dialect-aware",
        "On SQLite with `auth` configured but NO authorship fields, the server boots — the validator stays gated by `needsUsersTable(tables) && hasAuthConfig`",
        "On SQLite with `auth` configured AND an `updated-by` field, the server boots — `ensureUpdatedByTriggerFunction` early-returns on SQLite",
        "A mixed-case PostgreSQL scheme (`Postgres://`) routes to the PostgreSQL branch — boot does not fail with `Unsupported DATABASE_URL scheme` (RFC 3986: schemes are case-insensitive)",
        "A misrouted `DATABASE_URL` carrying a password is refused with the password redacted — the password reaches neither stdout nor stderr",
        "The redacted refusal stays diagnosable — it still names the scheme as typed, the host, the port and the database, with `***` standing in for the password alone",
        "No boot-failure path leaks the password: neither the unsupported-scheme refusal nor the unreachable-host failure emits it on any stream",
