      id: "US-INFRASTRUCTURE-OBSERVABILITY-ERROR-REPORTING",
      title: "Unhandled server errors are reported to a Sentry-protocol backend when a DSN is set",
      criteria: [
        "With `SENTRY_DSN` set, an unhandled server error POSTs a Sentry envelope to the DSN's `/api/<project_id>/envelope/` endpoint, with an `X-Sentry-Auth` header whose `sentry_key` equals the DSN public key",
        "The envelope's event item (`type: \"event\"`) contains an `exception.values[]` entry with the error type/value and a parsed `stacktrace.frames` array",
        "The event carries `release` = `sovrium@<version>`, an `environment` (from `SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT`, else `NODE_ENV`), and a `server_name`",
        "The event's request context includes the method and URL, but the `cookie` and `authorization` request headers are scrubbed and never appear in the payload",
        "Error reporting is fire-and-forget and non-fatal — the errored request still returns its normal 500 response and the server keeps serving subsequent requests",
        "A recurring error **singleton** (the same object instance re-thrown on separate requests) is reported again once past the 60 s fingerprint dedup window — the double-report guard collapses one error across two boundaries, it does NOT blacklist an object for the whole process lifetime",
        "A reported request failure carries a **request-scoped** stack — at least one frame from Sovrium's own source (the boundary that captured it) and no CLI-boot frame (`src/cli/index.ts`) — never a stack frozen at module-import time",
        "The event's `request.url` keeps its path and every query-parameter **name**, but every query-parameter **value** is replaced with `[REDACTED]` — so a credential passed in a query string (`?token=…`, `?code=…`) never reaches the error store",
        "A **caller-fault** driver rejection answered `400` (a `CHECK` / FK / NOT NULL violation) is NOT reported to the error store — only a genuine server fault on the same server is",
        "A **4xx `HTTPException` raised at the HTTP boundary** (a `zValidator` rejecting a malformed JSON body) is answered `400` with the canonical API error envelope and is NOT reported to the error store — only a genuine `500` on the same server is",
        "Full error-reporting workflow: envelope delivery + auth header, exception/stacktrace payload, release/environment metadata, header scrub, query-value redaction, fire-and-forget resilience, plus the recurring-singleton path (request-scoped stack + re-report past the dedup window)",
      ],
