  "form-conditional-logic": [
    {
      id: "US-FORMS-CONDITIONAL-LOGIC",
      title: "Conditional Visibility, Required, and Disabled",
      criteria: [
        "`visibleWhen` evaluates `{ field, operator, value }` on the server and drops the field from the submitted payload when false",
        "`visibleWhen` supports `and: [Rule, ...]` composition (all sub-rules must be true); a field whose composite rule is false is served with its wrapper marked `data-condition-hidden=\"true\"`",
        "`visibleWhen` supports `or: [Rule, ...]` composition (any sub-rule may be true); `and` and `or` may be nested",
        "`requiredWhen` makes a field required only when its rule evaluates true; an otherwise-optional field becomes required only at that moment",
        "A value posted for a field whose `disabledWhen` rule is true is stored, neither refused nor dropped; nothing renders the field read-only on a hosted form yet",
        "Hidden fields (via `visibleWhen` returning false) are excluded from validation: a `required: true` field that is hidden does not block submission",
        "The condition operators `eq`, `neq`, `contains`, `empty`, `notEmpty`, `gt`, `gte`, `lt`, `lte`, `in`, `notIn` are all supported and behave per the catalog",
        "A rule that references an unknown field name (`{ field: typo, operator: eq, value: 1 }`) fails app schema validation with an error naming the form and the typo",
        "An operator inappropriate for the referenced field type (e.g. `gte` on a single-line-text field) fails app schema validation with a clear type-mismatch error",
        "When a field is BOTH hidden by `visibleWhen` AND has a non-null `defaultValue`, the value is NOT submitted (visibleWhen wins; hidden-by-condition is treated as \"not part of this submission\")",
        "On a single-page hosted form, a field whose `visibleWhen` is false is hidden on load, appears when the submitter picks the value the rule names, and disappears again when they pick another",
        "A `required` field hidden by `visibleWhen` does not block the submit, and the same field blocks it while it is visible and empty",
        "A value typed into a field that is then hidden by its `visibleWhen` is neither posted by the browser nor stored",
        "`requiredWhen` switches the control's `required` state live as the submitter changes the field it references",
        "The server-rendered page already carries each field's condition state, evaluated against the `$query` prefill, so the form reads correctly before any script runs",
        "Conditions stay live on a page that embeds the form with `formRef`, and on a multi-step form a field can depend on an answer given on an earlier step",
      ],
    },
  ],
