        "A `$query` prefill or a literal `defaultValue` selects its own option, and the empty option is rendered without being selected",
        "An optional select left untouched submits empty and stores NULL rather than its first option",
        "A standalone select with `optionsSource` offers one choice per matching row — filtered and sorted — on a public form whose visitors have no read permission on the table",
        "A row added to the source table is offered on the next page load, with no redeploy",
        "The browser makes no records-API request for the choices, and no column other than the display and value columns reaches the served page",
        "A `table-field` over a `relationship` column renders a select of the related rows labelled by the column's `displayField`, stores the picked row's id, and does so on a later step of a multi-step form too",
        "An `optionsSource` on a relationship `table-field` overrides the default choices — its label column, filter and sort are honoured — on a single page and on a later step",
        "Structural mistakes in a form's choice source are refused when the config is loaded, naming the form and the field",
        "A choice source that would expose a read-restricted or sensitive column, or filter on `$currentUser` on a form without `access.require`, is refused when the config is loaded",
        "Choices read from a table are offered when the form is embedded in a page with `formRef` and when a dialog wraps it with `formRef`",
        "A markdown link in `helpText` renders as a link that opens in a new tab (`target=\"_blank\"`, `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`) and leaves the form, and what was typed in it, in place",
        "`helpText` renders bold, italic, inline code and line breaks, and leaves headings, lists and images unrendered",
        "Scripts, event handlers, raw HTML and `javascript:` or protocol-relative links in `helpText` never execute or reach the page, while a legitimate link beside them still renders",
        "A choice source whose `displayField` or `valueField` is a lookup or a rollup of an `email` column is refused when the config is loaded, naming the computed column and the column it reads",
        "A choice source whose label is a lookup of a column the related table restricts with `permissions.fields` is refused when the config is loaded, naming the column it reads",
        "A lookup of a plain text column is accepted as a choice label and renders, and no withheld column of either table reaches the served page",
        "A choice source whose label is a formula naming a sensitive column is refused when the config is loaded, naming the column the formula reads",
        "A choice source whose label the built-in default read rules hide from a `member` or a `viewer` is refused when the config is loaded",
        "A column the built-in default read rules leave readable, or that the table's own `permissions.fields` leaves unrestricted, is accepted as a choice label",
        "A hosted form over a `currency` column draws a number input with the currency symbol beside it, stepped by the column's precision and opening a decimal keypad, and the amount typed is stored as a number",
        "A hosted form over a `percentage` column draws a number input with a percent sign after it, bounded by the column's `min` and `max`, and stores the value typed on the column's own 0 to 100 scale",
        "A hosted form over a `rating` column draws a radio group of one choice per rank; the chosen rank is stored as a number, and choosing it again clears it so the record stores NULL, never 0",
        "A `section` entry renders its heading and description between the fields around it, in declared order, and adds nothing to what the form submits",
        "Every required field of a hosted form, whatever its control, shows a required mark beside its label and carries `aria-required=\"true\"`; an optional field carries neither",
        "Optional typed answers left empty on a hosted form — a relationship, a number, a currency, a percentage, a date, a single-select — create the row with those columns empty",
        "A `status` column on a hosted form is a select of its options, led by the empty option",
        "A `user` column on a hosted form offers a signed-in member the app's accounts by name, stores the chosen account's id, and left blank stores nothing",
        "An `email`, a `url` and a `phone-number` column left empty on a hosted form store no value rather than an empty string, and the answers a visitor gives are stored as typed",
        "A submitted relationship value outside the rows the form offers is answered as a missing row and stores nothing",
